The Bad Guys is a 2022 American animated heist comedy film loosely based on The Bad Guys
children's book series by Aaron Blabey, and produced by DreamWorks Animation.

12
00:54:32,727 --> 00:54:38,727
The film was directed by Pierre Perifel in his feature directorial debut, written by Etan Cohen, and stars the voices of Sam
Rockwell, Marc Maron, Awkwafina, Craig Robinson, Anthony Ramos, Richard Ayoade, Zazie Beetz, Alex Borstein, and Lilly Singh.

13
00:59:05,454 --> 00:59:11,454
It tells the story of a criminal group of anthropomorphic animals who, upon being caught, pretend to attempt to reform
themselves as model citizens, only for their leader to find himself genuinely drawn to changing his ways for good.

14
01:03:38,181 --> 01:03:44,181
Work on the film started in March 2018, with Cohen writing the screenplay.

15
01:08:10,909 --> 01:08:16,909
The characters and themes drew inspiration from various crime films and anime series such as Pulp Fiction (1994), the Ocean's film trilogy, Lupin III, and
Sherlock Hound, while the inspiration for the film's animation style came from Sony Pictures Animation's Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse (2018).

16
01:12:43,636 --> 01:12:49,636
Production began at DreamWorks Animation's Glendale campus, and some additional production assets were borrowed
from Jellyfish Pictures, with voice acting being done remotely due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

17
01:17:16,363 --> 01:17:22,363
The Bad Guys was released theatrically by Universal Pictures in several
countries on March 16, 2022, and in the United States on April 22.

18
01:21:49,090 --> 01:21:55,090
It received positive reviews from critics and grossed $250.8 million.

